       <section anchor="uniform-resource-identifiers" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-3.2">
         <name slugifiedName="name-uniform-resource-identifiers">Uniform Resource Identifiers</name>
         <t indent="0" pn="section-3.2-1">URIs have been known by many names: WWW addresses, Universal Document
-Identifiers, Universal Resource Identifiers [3], and finally the
-combination of Uniform Resource Locators (URL) [4] and Names (URN)
-[20]. As far as HTTP is concerned, Uniform Resource Identifiers are
+Identifiers, Universal Resource Identifiers <xref target="3" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="3"/>, and finally the
+combination of Uniform Resource Locators (URL) <xref target="4" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="4"/> and Names (URN)
+<xref target="20" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="20"/>. As far as HTTP is concerned, Uniform Resource Identifiers are
